== Preserved distinctions from canonical research synopsis ==

The canonical research taxonomy distinguishes episodic future simulation (subjective detail, not forecast accuracy), counterfactual simulation (imagined changes, not identified interventions), the simulation heuristic (construction ease, not objective likelihood), and motor/action rehearsal (task- and protocol-dependent transfer). These are distinct experimental traditions, not interchangeable observations of a single faculty.

A rigorous protocol records stimulus selection, baseline, individual differences, scenario coding, assessor blinding, demand characteristics, behavioral outcomes and uncertainty. A single unrealized imagined event does not invalidate a probabilistic forecast: forecast calibration requires repeated comparable cases. The analogy to computational trajectory generation is functional, not evidence of human-like imagery or consciousness.

